Third-Party Components are licensed to you by their owners under their own license terms, which are included with the Software or identified in its notices (for example node-LICENSE.txt and the files ending in .LEGAL.txt). Those terms, and not Sections 2 to 4 of this Agreement, govern your use of the Third-Party Components, and nothing in this Agreement limits any right those terms give you. Sections 17 and 18 apply to the Third-Party Components as they do to the rest of the Software, and Rotavox provides them "AS IS".

14. NO SUPPORT OBLIGATION

Rotavox has no obligation under this Agreement to support, maintain, correct or update the Software, or to keep it compatible with any version of Windows, RadioDJ or any other product. Any support, update or help that Rotavox chooses to give is given under this Agreement and may be changed or stopped at any time.

15. VERIFICATION AND SUSPENSION

The Software reports its version, its Runner Key and how it is being used to the Rotavox Service, and Rotavox may use that information to check that you are complying with this Agreement. Rotavox may suspend the Software or a Runner Key at once, without notice, if it reasonably believes that you have breached this Agreement, that a Runner Key has been disclosed or misused, or that suspension is needed to protect the Rotavox Service, another station or anyone's rights.

16. TERM AND TERMINATION

16.1 Term. This Agreement starts when you first accept it or first download, install or use the Software, whichever comes first, and continues until it ends under this Section.

16.2 By you. You may end this Agreement at any time by uninstalling the Software and destroying every copy of it.

16.3 Automatically. This Agreement and your license end automatically, without notice, if you breach Section 2, 4, 5 or 10, or when your right to use the Rotavox Service for the Station ends for any reason.

16.4 By Rotavox. Rotavox may end this Agreement or suspend your license at any time by giving you notice. While Section 7 applies, it may do so without notice.

16.5 What happens then. When this Agreement ends, every right it gives you ends. You must stop using the Software at once, uninstall it, destroy every copy in your possession or control, and, if Rotavox asks, confirm in writing that you have done so. Ending this Agreement does not limit any other remedy Rotavox has.

16.6 Survival. Sections 1, 3, 4, 8.1, 10, 11, 12, 16.5 and 16.6, and Sections 17 through 28, survive the end of this Agreement, as does any other term that by its nature should.

